The story is based in part on various short stories by Clarke, including "The Sentinel" (written in 1948 for a BBC competition, but first published in 1951 under the title "Sentinel of Eternity"). The first part of the novel, in which aliens influence the primitive ancestors of humans, is similar to the plot of Clarke''s 1953 short story "Encounter in the Dawn".
By 1992, the novel had sold three million copies worldwide.

